 "parts": [
  "Hot leftovers? Grandma said let them cool first.",
  "That rule may come from the icebox. Hot food melted the ice.",
  "And ice was precious until the next delivery.",
  "Today, fridges make their own cold.",
  "So which rule is right?",
  "In the U.S., North Dakota State University says hot food can go straight in.",
  "Big pot of soup? Split it into shallow containers.",
  "But Britain's Food Standards Agency says: don't place hot or warm food in your fridge.",
  "Cool it first, then fridge it within two hours.",
  "Two rules, one thing in common: never leave it out overnight."
